{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:8e5e8b70023d4f2d5a6c2f7101052fc7fe40fca1fc772496fe350ec1858904d0","title":"The geometry separates a potentially GUT-sized SO(4) plane from four smaller compact dimensions. This permits an intermediate six-dimensional description with locally unified boundary symmetry and a smaller four-dimensional gauge group.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0002"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8e9bc25fdc64711af630f81002565ff4b0924596f8d6ebf6e1b5c5f7a6ac425e","title":"Can perturbative type II compactifications produce supersymmetric AdS4 extrema with finite main moduli, and can their sources form domain walls connecting an AdS4 region to flat spacetime?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0002"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8eb1b2176838f1b047679652e84dd30f0d61ebca1b9a8313e91a95bfdca6f6c1","title":"Can a perturbatively stabilized flux compactification nevertheless decay through a smooth bubble of nothing, and what charged source permits the compact cycle to disappear without a flux singularity?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0008"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8e08e16773f081bc1d1fd0d5a44841e6cfd9b65ea50309c95dd1514681674e19","title":"What replaces ordinary bifundamental matter between ADE gauge factors, and how can its tensor branches, partial Higgs branches, circle reductions and wall counterparts be characterized?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0017"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8e902d54f2f73f38c303ad3fd9cef07069292bea556223c0499eefc584a9d806","title":"How should the proposed exclusion of stable non-supersymmetric large-radius AdS be formulated using branes in noncompact space, and do non-supersymmetric CFT counterexamples yield supers