ination-details-fine-0073"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8e3606430be2f9fe635f1aa46752fb414c896b0c24599fc3f11ba08eb37101c5","title":"Does the tadpole cost of stabilizing many complex-structure moduli remain proportional to the number stabilized at smooth, discrete-symmetry loci in the interior of moduli space, especially for invariant flux with nonzero on-shell superpotential?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0078"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8ee125ca8b082944d42f99fef969e47a2bcc4f5e257f538b05e8ed257f5349ea","title":"Can dRGT massive gravity describe a parametrically broad energy interval above graviton mass m while satisfying finite-momentum-transfer positivity, and can detuned potentials, higher derivatives or non-gravitational spin-2 interactions evade the resulting restriction?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0081"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8ec23ec6c790416e0988fc283acec9a50b17b621620173f324e53e09f74f6002","title":"Which additional supersymmetric and non-supersymmetric type IIA AdS4 flux-vacuum branches admit parametric separation from the compactification scale, and can asymmetric flux rescalings generate such families beyond twisted toroidal examples?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0083"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8e20c0326768a1f649bdfd14b44bd23e09092673cf36a5ad36fe7532ac92f1c6","title":"Which parameters of a quartic dark-sector tunnelling potential permit a Dark Big Bang under the cosmological bounds adopted in the paper, and can the newly identified parameter region produce all dark matter with observable gravitational-wave signatures?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0089"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8efbe22eb5bdd3b4be6642d735251733c70df956215b51c31b60ae3de216cbbf","titl